# wsm settings: shipped by core/wsm. Every setting wsm reads (anfs's own are in ~/.config/anfs/anfs.env).
#
# This machine's values go in ~/.config/wsm/wsm.local.env, beside this file (yours, never shipped).
# The environment wins over both: `WSM_SPACES_HOME=/tmp/s wsm ls` does what it says. Format:
# NAME=value, one per line, read and never sourced (only a leading ~/, or a value that is ~, is
# expanded, to $HOME; a value may be quoted). A commented line is the default used when nothing
# sets it; an active one is what the package sets. `wsm config list` shows them and where each is
# from; `wsm config set NAME=value` writes wsm.local.env.

# The one root `wsm install` links every source's spaces into (<root>/<source>/<path>)
#WSM_SPACES_HOME=~/spaces
